{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"chewy-flavoury-milksnake","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Observation\nOn 2026-11-10 (~20:00 PST) `scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py 3344 --revision <full sha>` exited 1, yet Gerrit reports change 3344 MERGED and its merge commit 9f8b2af21c8eff24ba85f9625fcc6d80f77d5742 is on origin/main. The script's stderr/traceback was not captured.\n\nThe script has no explicit `return 1`: exit 1 means an exception escaped `main()`. Paths that can raise after the votes are checked: the optional hashtag POST, the revision-scoped submit POST re-raising a non-409 `HTTPError`, or a `URLError`/timeout from `_request`. Which one fired is unknown.\n\n## Impact\nA caller (agent or human) that trusts the exit code concludes the submit failed after the change already landed, and may retry, re-push (destroying votes on a merged change's successor) or report a false failure.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n1. The submit POST returned a non-2xx (e.g. 5xx or a proxy timeout) after Gerrit committed the merge.\n2. A client-side timeout fired while Gerrit was merging (Rebase-If-Necessary can be slow).\n3. An exception from the hashtag POST or response parsing.\n\n## Approach\n1. Reproduce or recover the failure mode: check Gerrit's httpd/error log for the 3344 submit request around 2026-11-11T03:5x–04:1xZ (read-only), and test `_request` against a stubbed submit that times out/5xxs after merging.\n2. Make the script reconcile on any non-409 submit error: re-read the change; if status is MERGED at the requested revision, print that and exit 0; otherwise report the original error with a non-zero code. No new config key/env var/flag.\n3. Unit tests for: merged-despite-error → 0; error and not merged → non-zero with the HTTP body; 409 path unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The root cause of the 3344 exit 1 is identified with evidence (log line or deterministic reproduction), or the reconciliation covers every exception path after the vote check, with a test per path.\n- [ ] A submit that raises after Gerrit merged the requested revision exits 0 and says it merged.\n- [ ] A submit that fails without merging still exits non-zero and prints Gerrit's response body.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.","id":"fd1a-4c91-151f-4e1d","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"gerrit_safe_submit.py exits 1 although Gerrit merged the change"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794370756550300379,"uuid":"258dadcc-5f14-47e0-af13-a1a44004f8d6"}